%S A398446 2,6,23,92,373,1520,6206,25352,103553,422792,1725202,7035176,28669778,
%T A398446 116759232,475208828,1932928592,7857747353,31925996792,129648659018,
%U A398446 526236855272,2134990895318,8658117748832,35097330068708,142218971547632,576080138077178,2332698443549840
%N A398446 Number of permutations of [n] avoiding the pattern 1324 with the maximum element n in position n-2.
%C A398446 Inserting the maximum at position k preserves 1324-avoidance exactly when the prefix of length k-1 avoids 132, so a(n) counts the 1324-avoiders of length n-1 whose first n-3 entries avoid 132.
%C A398446 a(n) = A000984(n-2) + c(n), where c(n) counts the 1324-avoiders of length n-1 whose longest 132-avoiding prefix has length exactly n-3, and c(n) = (M^2-4*M-1)*binomial(2*M,M)/(2*(M+1)) + 4^M/2 with M = n-3; c(3) = c(4) = 0, then 3, 22, 121, 596, 2774, 12482, ... The A000984(n-2) term counts those whose first n-2 entries also avoid 132: any 1324 occurrence in a word of length n-1 has its first three positions among the first n-2, so such a word avoids 1324 automatically, giving A000108(n-2) prefixes times n-1 final values, and (n-1)*A000108(n-2) = A000984(n-2).
%C A398446 Conjecture: for d >= 1, A395725(n,n-d) = p_d(M)*binomial(2*M,M) + q_d(M)*4^M with M = n-1-d, where deg p_d = d-1 with leading coefficient 1/d!, q_1 = 0, and for d >= 2, deg q_d = d-2 with leading coefficient binomial(d,2)/d!, p_d(0) - q_d(0) = 1, and p_d(0) + q_d(0) = A061552(d). Verified for d = 1..9. This sequence is d = 2, where those conditions leave nothing free: p_2 = (M+3)/2 and q_2 = 1/2. The next case is d = 3, with p_3 = (M^2+11*M+21)/6 and q_3 = (M+5)/2.
%F A398446 a(n) = (n*binomial(2*n-6, n-3) + 4^(n-3))/2.
%F A398446 a(n) = A395725(n,n-2).
%F A398446 G.f.: Sum_{n>=3} a(n)*x^(n-3) = (5*s^2 + 2*s + 1)/(4*s^3), where s = sqrt(1-4*x).
%F A398446 (n-3)*(n-7)*a(n) = 2*(4*n^2-41*n+96)*a(n-1) - 8*(2*n-9)*(n-6)*a(n-2) for n >= 5.
%F A398446 a(n) ~ 2^(2*n-7)*sqrt(n/Pi). - _Stefano Spezia_, Jul 30 2026
%e A398446 a(4) = 6: every permutation of [4] with 4 in position 2 avoids 1324, namely 1423, 1432, 2413, 2431, 3412, 3421.
%t A398446 avoids1324[p_] := !AnyTrue[Subsets[Range[Length[p]], {4}], p[[#[[1]]]] < p[[#[[3]]]] < p[[#[[2]]]] < p[[#[[4]]]] &]; a[n_] := Count[Permutations[Range[n]], p_ /; p[[n-2]] == n && avoids1324[p]]; Table[a[n], {n, 3, 9}]
%o A398446 (Python)
%o A398446 from itertools import permutations, combinations
%o A398446 def avoids1324(p):
%o A398446     return not any(p[i]<p[k]<p[j]<p[l] for i, j, k, l in combinations(range(len(p)), 4))
%o A398446 def a(n): return sum(1 for p in permutations(range(1, n+1)) if p[n-3]==n and avoids1324(p))
%o A398446 print([a(n) for n in range(3, 10)])
%Y A398446 Cf. A000108, A000984, A061552, A391315, A395725.
%K A398446 nonn,easy,new
%O A398446 3,1
